+
+Range threads (plan §2 #116): `range.ts` (`RangeController`) shows the review's threads as block rows inside its two read-only columns; Vue fills them through the hosts `RangeEvents.hosts` hands out, never through the editor. `internal/threadAnchor.ts` (`anchorAt`, `linePlace`) is the one rule from a column line to a `ThreadLine` and to its partner line; `threadRows.ts` (pure) groups the shown threads by aligned place (a removed or added line's gap after its difference's other side, an unchanged line's after its partner; collapsed threads place no row) and `rowHeight` (the larger column's summed host heights); `threadField.ts` holds each column's rows and count marks from `showThreadRows` and provides one `block` widget per row (`side: 1 + k` at the end of line `place − 1`, before line 1 for place 0), plus `threadAnchors` (the text lines around each unchanged row in both columns) that `CompareFrame` merges, sorted, into its scroll anchors; `threadWidget.ts` (`ThreadRowWidget`) `eq`s by row key, column and keys only, so a height change keeps its DOM; `threadHosts.ts` (`ThreadHosts`) keeps one host per shown key for as long as the key is shown, one `ResizeObserver` on every host (disconnected hosts skipped) writes the row height on both cells and calls `requestMeasure`, writes `--thread-left`/`--thread-width` on each column host (the rows are `position: sticky`), and gives focus back to a field inside a host after CodeMirror re-attaches it; `threadNumbers.ts` merges a `mousedown` into the number gutter (a number starts a thread, the count badge toggles that line's threads) and draws the number plus the badge as a `lineNumberMarkers` marker; the hover icon is a `theme.css` mask from `--thread-icon`.
